# DropCode-P2P — environment reference
#
# The signaling server now runs on Cloudflare Workers (signaling-worker/),
# which does NOT read a .env file at runtime — there is no server process
# to load one into. This file exists only as a reference for where each old
# value now lives.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plain (non-secret) values — set in signaling-worker/wrangler.toml under
# [vars], and applied on every `npx wrangler deploy`:
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS          comma-separated browser origins allowed to open
#                             a WebSocket connection, e.g.
#                             https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io
#                             (this project's frontend is deployed to GitHub
#                             Pages — see the root README.md, Part 4)
#   ROOM_TTL_MINUTES          how long an unclaimed transfer code stays valid
#   MAX_JOIN_ATTEMPTS         failed join-room attempts allowed per IP
#   LOCKOUT_WINDOW_MINUTES    rolling window the attempt count is measured over
#   LOCKOUT_DURATION_MINUTES  how long an IP is locked out after tripping the limit
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets — set via `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>` from inside
# signaling-worker/ (never committed to source control, not in wrangler.toml):
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   CF_TURN_KEY_ID     Cloudflare Realtime TURN key uid (preferred TURN path
#   CF_TURN_API_TOKEN  — short-lived credentials, minted fresh per request;
#                        see root README.md, Part 2, for how to create these)
#
#   TURN_URLS          fallback for a non-Cloudflare TURN provider, only used
#   TURN_USERNAME       if CF_TURN_KEY_ID/CF_TURN_API_TOKEN are unset — comma-
#   TURN_CREDENTIAL      separated URL(s), e.g. turn:host:3478?transport=udp,
#                        turn:host:3478?transport=tcp,turns:host:5349?transport=tcp
#                        (static/long-lived; all three must be set together)
#
# Leave all five unset to run STUN-only.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No longer applicable (was Node/ws-server-only, has no Workers equivalent):
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   PORT           — Workers has no listening port to configure
#   TRUST_PROXY    — Workers has no raw socket; the Worker reads the
#                     Cloudflare-set CF-Connecting-IP header directly instead
#
# See signaling-worker/README.md for exact commands.
